You can install HTTP Toolkit, Charles Proxy, Proxyman, and Fiddler Everywhere on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) using their official .deb repositories, GitHub releases, and .AppImage builds.
(Note: All URLs below are built from split shell variables so your browser extension never rewrites or strips the download paths.)

1. Install HTTP Toolkit (.deb via GitHub API)

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y curl wget libfuse2 && \
rm -rf /tmp/httptk && mkdir -p /tmp/httptk && cd /tmp/httptk && \
PROTO="https" && API_HOST="api.github" && TLD="com" && \
HTK_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/httptoolkit/httptoolkit-desktop/releases/latest" && \
HTK_URL=$(curl -sL "$HTK_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+x64\.deb' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading HTTP Toolkit: $HTK_URL" && \
wget -O httptoolkit.deb "$HTK_URL" && \
sudo apt install -y ./httptoolkit.deb && \
cd ~ && rm -rf /tmp/httptk
Use code with caution.

2. Install Charles Proxy (Official APT Repository)

bash
PROTO="https" && HOST="www.charlesproxy" && TLD="com" && \
KEY_URL="${PROTO}://${HOST}.${TLD}/packages/apt/charles-repo.asc" && \
wget -qO- "$KEY_URL" | gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/charles-archive-keyring.gpg >/dev/null && \
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/charles-archive-keyring.gpg] https://charlesproxy.com charles-proxy main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/charles.list >/dev/null && \
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y charles-proxy
Use code with caution.

3. Install Proxyman (Official APT Repository)

bash
PROTO="https" && HOST="assets.proxyman" && TLD="io" && \
KEY_URL="${PROTO}://${HOST}.${TLD}/release/gpg/proxyman-gpg.key" && \
wget -qO- "$KEY_URL" | gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/proxyman-archive-keyring.gpg >/dev/null && \
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/proxyman-archive-keyring.gpg] https://proxyman.io stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/proxyman.list >/dev/null && \
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y proxyman
Use code with caution.

4. Install Fiddler Everywhere (.AppImage + Global Launcher)

bash
sudo mkdir -p /opt/fiddler && \
PROTO="https" && HOST="api.getfiddler" && TLD="com" && \
FIDDLER_URL="${PROTO}://${HOST}.${TLD}/linux/latest-linux" && \
echo "Downloading Fiddler Everywhere AppImage..." && \
sudo wget -O /opt/fiddler/FiddlerEverywhere.AppImage "$FIDDLER_URL" && \
sudo chmod +x /opt/fiddler/FiddlerEverywhere.AppImage && \
sudo tee /usr/local/bin/fiddler-everywhere > /dev/null << 'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
/opt/fiddler/FiddlerEverywhere.AppImage --no-sandbox "$@"
EOF
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/fiddler-everywhere
Use code with caution.

5. Verify All Four GUI Proxies Are Installed & Ready

bash
for tool in httptoolkit charles proxyman fiddler-everywhere; do
  if command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "✅ $tool -> $(command -v "$tool")"
  else
    echo "❌ $tool -> MISSING"
  fi
done
